Hosting

Hosting means making your application or website available on the internet.

======

| Service               | Explanation                                                                                 |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **EC2**               | You manually manage and run your application on a virtual server                            |
| **Lightsail**         | A simpler AWS hosting option for beginners and small applications                           |
| **Elastic Beanstalk** | Helps deploy and manage an application without manually handling much of the infrastructure |


=======

🖥️ EC2

You manage:
Server + OS + Application

More control, but you have more responsibility.

====

💡 Lightsail

Simple setup
     ↓
Choose application/server
     ↓
Deploy

Suitable for simple websites and small applications.

=====

☁️ Elastic Beanstalk

Upload Application
        ↓
Elastic Beanstalk
        ↓
AWS handles deployment infrastructure
        ↓
Application runs

=====

EC2 = Virtual Server
Lightsail = Simple Hosting
Elastic Beanstalk = Easy Application Deployment and Hosting

EC2 provides the underlying virtual computer, while Lightsail simplifies server setup and Elastic Beanstalk simplifies application deployment, so 
the three options differ mainly in how much infrastructure you manage for the same hosting goal.
